draft_notes.limitations:
Several tie-breaks are reproduced faithfully but cannot be exercised, because the generator rejects those cases:
- an ambiguous left colour;
- equal-size left objects;
- the largest left object being equally near both candidates.

The background is taken as palette[0], following the generator, which always uses black. Out-of-bounds placements are clipped, as in the original, although valid scenes always fit. Scenes with other than two objects per colour are handled with the same generic pairing as the archived solver. I found no contradiction between the fixtures and the rule. I have not run any tests.
